/fetch/$s_!v0nk!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F46fc2cf0-7745-4c27-8875-94a97cb1fc9f_900x900.png&quot;,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;youtube_url&quot;:null,&quot;show_links&quot;:null,&quot;feed_url&quot;:null}"></div><p>To err is human.</p><p>Enjoy it early,</p><p>best</p><p>Azeem</p>]]></content:encoded></item><item><title><![CDATA[🔮 AI politics & the future of growth ++ #602]]></title><description><![CDATA[Plus: Fruit fly mines bitcoin, easy energy & AI-generated TV]]></description><link>https://www.exponentialview.co/p/ev-602</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.exponentialview.co/p/ev-602</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[Azeem Azhar]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 14:22:55 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!614H!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcac3090d-4843-4ef0-8ec8-618d7447e936_4608x3072.jpeg" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Hi all, </p><p>The past ten days have felt like the AI pot finally boiled over. It&#8217;s a complicated and confusing moment. We have to hold in our heads that most Americans appear to loathe AI, but businesses and consumers seem to like it enough that Anthropic is well on its way to $100bn in annualised revenue this year. And despite being on track to be the fastest-growing company ever, Anthropic&#8217;s leadership believes they might kill all their customers. And there is more besides. If you haven&#8217;t already, read my essay on the <a href="https://www.exponentialview.co/p/ai-doesnt-need-a-mind-to-run-amok">emerging control risks from AI</a>. </p><p>I&#8217;m also increasingly concerned about the security situation in Europe after coordinated messages from several countries about the likelihood of substantial Russian aggression. I will cover that in the next few issues, after I get back from Hong Kong where I am this week. </p><p>But meanwhile, let&#8217;s try to make sense of the swirling cauldron that is AI.</p><p>Azeem </p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2" target="_blank" href="https://www.exponentialview.co/subscribe" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!AS0p!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe97c85d4-1fdb-4de4-ad6f-244a41ecd8e8_1969x799.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!AS0p!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe97c85d4-1fdb-4de4-ad6f-244a41ecd8e8_1969x799.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!AS0p!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe97c85d4-1fdb-4de4-ad6f-244a41ecd8e8_1969x799.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!AS0p!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe97c85d4-1fdb-4de4-ad6f-244a41ecd8e8_1969x799.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!AS0p!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe97c85d4-1fdb-4de4-ad6f-244a41ecd8e8_1969x799.png" width="535" height="217.16002747252747" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/e97c85d4-1fdb-4de4-ad6f-244a41ecd8e8_1969x799.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:591,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:535,&quot;bytes&quot;:1399379,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;https://www.exponentialview.co/subscribe&quot;,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://www.exponentialview.co/i/216277536?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe97c85d4-1fdb-4de4-ad6f-244a41ecd8e8_1969x799.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!AS0p!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe97c85d4-1fdb-4de4-ad6f-244a41ecd8e8_1969x799.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!AS0p!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe97c85d4-1fdb-4de4-ad6f-244a41ecd8e8_1969x799.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!AS0p!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe97c85d4-1fdb-4de4-ad6f-244a41ecd8e8_1969x799.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!AS0p!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe97c85d4-1fdb-4de4-ad6f-244a41ecd8e8_1969x799.png 1456w" sizes="100vw" fetchpriority="high"></picture><div></div></div></a></figure></div><h3><strong>Americans hate AI. Who&#8217;s to blame?</strong></h3><p>More than one in six Americans believe AI <a href="https://x.com/binarybits/status/2100620997808312600">will almost certainly destroy humanity</a>. Last month I wrote about the <a href="https://www.exponentialview.co/p/the-problem-with-petards">petard problem of AI </a></p><blockquote><p>Today&#8217;s petardiers are not Rosencrantz and Guildenstern conspiring against the Prince of Denmark.</p><p>They are the titans of AI, the bosses of the labs, the investors behind them. For nearly a decade, these software coders had made promises: of reigniting economic growth, of making daily life easier and less risky, perhaps even of eliminating disease. To do this, they would need capital: to write their software and to build 21st-century infrastructure to run it. The gains will be so huge that they&#8217;d need to go quickly, very quickly.</p></blockquote><p>It got worse since then. Jacob Coxon&#8217;s <a href="https://x.com/hilbertspaess/status/2097476196791709843?s=20">viral tweet</a> uncorked the box where many were hiding their suspicions.</p><div class="twitter-embed" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://x.com/binarybits/status/2100620997808312600?s=20&quot;,&quot;full_text&quot;:&quot;This is wild. (I would have said \&quot;very small risk.\&quot;) <a class=\&quot;tweet-url\&quot; href=\&quot;https://www.politico.com/news/2026/09/16/poll-ai-technology-risks-humanity-trump-voters-01078087\&quot;>politico.com/news/2026/09/1&#8230;</a> &quot;,&quot;username&quot;:&quot;binarybits&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Timothy B. Lee&quot;,&quot;profile_image_url&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/profile_images/2069067922564435968/u8U3FKQE_normal.jpg&quot;,&quot;date&quot;:&quot;2026-09-17T16:20:48.000Z&quot;,&quot;photos&quot;:[{&quot;img_url&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/media/HSbnFcDWEAAuEqq.jpg&quot;,&quot;link_url&quot;:&quot;https://t.co/zXAcFx4ybQ&quot;}],&quot;quoted_tweet&quot;:{},&quot;reply_count&quot;:15,&quot;retweet_count&quot;:4,&quot;like_count&quot;:57,&quot;impression_count&quot;:59743,&quot;expanded_url&quot;:null,&quot;video_url&quot;:null,&quot;video_preview_media_key&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true}" data-component-name="Twitter2ToDOM"></div><p>Americans have never been wild about AI. In 2020, the Edelman Trust Barometer found that only 34% of Americans believed AI would have a positive impact, while 23% thought it would be largely negative. By 2024, mood had soured. Edelman reported that only 19% of Americans would embrace AI while 50% would object to it.<a class="footnote-anchor" data-component-name="FootnoteAnchorToDOM" id="footnote-anchor-1" href="#footnote-1" target="_self">1</a> </p><p>Two years of news coverage, a construction boom later, and chatbots that a quarter of American adults use daily &#8211; and this is where you get to? </p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!614H!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcac3090d-4843-4ef0-8ec8-618d7447e936_4608x3072.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!614H!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcac3090d-4843-4ef0-8ec8-618d7447e936_4608x3072.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!614H!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcac3090d-4843-4ef0-8ec8-618d7447e936_4608x3072.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!614H!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcac3090d-4843-4ef0-8ec8-618d7447e936_4608x3072.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!614H!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcac3090d-4843-4ef0-8ec8-618d7447e936_4608x3072.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!614H!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcac3090d-4843-4ef0-8ec8-618d7447e936_4608x3072.jpeg" width="533" height="355.45535714285717" data-