idden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class="image-caption"><span>Photo by </span><a href="https://unsplash.com/@kucz?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Nathan Kuczmarski</a><span> on </span><a href="https://unsplash.com/photos/protesters-hold-signs-against-ai-and-killer-robots-5HcL5noETmY?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Unsplash</a></figcaption></figure></div><p>Nearly a trillion dollars in the ground, to turn your customers against you. It doesn&#8217;t matter that <span class="mention-wrap" data-attrs="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Erik Brynjolfsson&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:4029135,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:null,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/02c6aa6f-ae6f-492a-8802-9bf7c5a8e3a5_1137x1137.jpeg&quot;,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;c0de8698-830f-49d4-981b-5a9793841682&quot;}" data-component-name="MentionToDOM"></span>&#8217;s research shows that the aggregate consumer surplus from AI in America is <a href="https://digitaleconomy.stanford.edu/publication/what-is-generative-ai-worth/">about $172 billion</a>.</p><p>But even with a lack of enthusiasm, to put it mildly, people will keep buying AI tools. My local barber, a four-chair shop, just installed an AI receptionist to handle bookings. The couple of hundred IT execs I spoke to in Las Vegas two weeks ago were unanimous in continuing with implementations.</p><p>If American businesses keep buying and American voters hate it, this will end up settled in the political arena. </p><p>Here are some of the more interesting things I&#8217;ve read on this matter:</p><ul><li><p><span class="mention-wrap" data-attrs="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ben Goertzel&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:312261,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:null,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://bucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/85762f14-9217-4410-96cf-3c6a84c88918_48x48.png&quot;,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;df52cda0-4053-40e0-986c-f69bd0aade38&quot;}" data-component-name="MentionToDOM"></span> <span>who coined the term AGI, challenges the labs&#8217; call for a centralized slowdown&nbsp;</span><a href="https://bengoertzel.substack.com/p/the-depth-psychology-of-darios-precalculatedly?r=cggcj&amp;utm_medium=ios"><span>in favor of a decentralized prosocial approach.</span> </a></p></li><li><p>Jaron Lanier, a VR pioneer, <a href="https://x.com/jimstewartson/status/2100253603969826831?s=20">spoke</a> at the AI event hosted by Steve Bannon and Bernie Sanders. He argued that the language we use when we talk about AI frames it as a super-powerful &#8216;being&#8217;. Ultimately, that choice of words cedes the terrain.</p></li><li><p>Mustafa Suleyman: &#8220;<a href="https://mustafa-suleyman.ai/a-warning-about-model-welfare">AI&#8217;s do not have rights, feelings or consciousness</a>. We must not train them to act as though they do.&#8221; </p><div><hr></div><p><mark data-color="#fff2cc" style="background-color: rgb(255, 242, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">For subscribers:</mark></p><ol><li><p><mark data-color="#fff2cc" style="background-color: rgb(255, 242, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">What do experts think will happen to economic growth under AI? And what do I think?</mark></p></li><li><p><mark data-color="#fff2cc" style="background-color: rgb(255, 242, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Planning for American AI supremacy</mark></p></li><li><p><mark data-color="#fff2cc" style="background-color: rgb(255, 242, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Fruit flies playing </mark><em><mark data-color="#fff2cc" style="background-color: rgb(255, 242, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Doom </mark></em><mark data-color="#fff2cc" style="background-color: rgb(255, 242, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">and more</mark></p></li></ol><div><hr></div></li></ul><h3><strong>The new growth equilibrium?</strong></h3>
