   ]]></content:encoded></item><item><title><![CDATA[🫧 Is AI a bubble yet? Our five gauges say no]]></title><description><![CDATA[Demand is justifying all the spending, but the spending is getting harder to unwind]]></description><link>https://www.exponentialview.co/p/is-ai-a-bubble-yet-our-five-gauges</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.exponentialview.co/p/is-ai-a-bubble-yet-our-five-gauges</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[Azeem Azhar]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 12:05:40 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7X20!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F63e90d79-bb3e-4929-b41d-f897d19dd566_2576x1450.png" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Is AI a bubble? Not yet. Our updated dashboard tracking the investment wave currently has no gauges in the red, two in amber, and the rest in healthy green (just). </p><p>Since our last update, AI revenues have continued to rise, reaching $126 billion over the last twelve months as of July.  We also experienced a jumpy market, which led to a severe correction in semiconductor stocks, somewhat cooling public valuations. On our side, we have improved the methodology for counting AI capex (we show both the published and restated series below).</p><p>That demand has smacked headlong into a tight supply of compute capacity, which is being met by increasing investment in infrastructure. And with that comes more risk.  While the hyperscalers are still using a large share of their cash reserves, they are increasingly scouring the globe for capital, both straight-up debt and increasingly intricate financing vehicles. As <span class="mention-wrap" data-attrs="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Michael Parekh&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:37467,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:null,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://bucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/608453d4-b43c-4981-929c-ac64bd59c50c_400x400.jpeg&quot;,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;39d41ec5-3210-454c-ab03-b07309d92525&quot;}" data-component-name="MentionToDOM"></span> argues, this &#8220;<a href="https://michaelparekh.substack.com/p/gaming-the-system-for-ai-nvidia-openai">gaming of the system</a>&#8221; is not only rational; it is necessary, as long as revenue is compounding. But these structures can become brittle if it slows. </p><p>Funding quality has deteriorated since Sep 2025. In our base case, we expect it and economic strain to turn red during 2027. </p><p>The full analysis shows where the tension is building.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7X20!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F63e90d79-bb3e-4929-b41d-f897d19dd566_2576x1450.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7X20!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F63e90d79-bb3e-4929-b41d-f897d19dd566_2576x1450.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7X20!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F63e90d79-bb3e-4929-b41d-f897d19dd566_2576x1450.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7X20!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F63e90d79-bb3e-4929-b41d-f897d19dd566_2576x1450.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7X20!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F63e90d79-bb3e-4929-b41d-f897d19dd566_2576x1450.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substack