   ]]></content:encoded></item><item><title><![CDATA[🔮 The market misread Google’s AI exodus]]></title><description><![CDATA[We're earlier in the cycle than you may think]]></description><link>https://www.exponentialview.co/p/google-deepmind-exodus-ai-cycle</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.exponentialview.co/p/google-deepmind-exodus-ai-cycle</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[Azeem Azhar]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 04:31:21 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!JwUN!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F23b429b9-5d55-4175-a220-ba8b436a5c6d_2700x1500.png" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><a href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/05/technology/google-researchers-ai-startup.html"><span>Jeff Dean and Sanjay Ghemawat </span></a><span>are leaving Google after more than a quarter-century, as you know. Outside the industry, the pair may not be well-known, but theirs was &#8220;</span><a href="https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2018/12/10/the-friendship-that-made-google-huge"><span>the friendship that made Google huge</span></a><span>.&#8221; Jeff and Sanjay are the reason why billions of us have been able to use Google over the past 20 years. Their work on distributed systems, in particular, is why the search engine could handle decades of growth. &#8220;Sanjay and I sped up Google Search by 10% today,&#8221; Dean once told his daughter.</span></p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-131!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66125f16-10fe-4503-923a-6e43537dc179_1296x1284.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-131!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66125f16-10fe-4503-923a-6e43537dc179_1296x1284.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-131!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66125f16-10fe-4503-923a-6e43537dc179_1296x1284.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-131!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66125f16-10fe-4503-923a-6e43537dc179_1296x1284.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-131!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66125f16-10fe-4503-923a-6e43537dc179_1296x1284.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-131!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66125f16-10fe-4503-923a-6e43537dc179_1296x1284.png" width="461" height="456.73148148148147" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/66125f16-10fe-4503-923a-6e43537dc179_1296x1284.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1284,&quot;width&quot;:1296,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:461,&quot;bytes&quot;:4235432,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://www.exponentialview.co/i/211191094?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66125f16-10fe-4503-923a-6e43537dc179_1296x1284.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-131!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66125f16-10fe-4503-923a-6e43537dc179_1296x1284.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-131!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66125f16-10fe-4503-923a-6e43537dc179_1296x1284.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-131!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66125f16-10fe-4503-923a-6e43537dc179_1296x1284.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-131!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66125f16-10fe-4503-923a-6e43537dc179_1296x1284.png 1456w" sizes="100vw" fetchpriority="high"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class="image-caption"><a href="https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2018/12/10/the-friendship-that-made-google-huge">Illustration by David Plunkert in The New Yorker</a><em><a href="https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2018/12/10/the-friendship-that-made-google-huge">,</a></em><a href="https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2018/12/10/the-friendship-that-made-google-huge"> published on December 3, 2018</a></figcaption></figure></div><p><span>They weren&#8217;t alone. DeepMind&#8217;s founder and Nobel Laureate Demis Hassabis also wanted to leave the company, </span><a href="https://pathfounders.com/p/pathfounders-newsletter-our-sources-say-hassabis-wants-out"><span>according to well-grounded reports</span></a><span>. He was persuaded to stay in a chair role for the sake of the share price. Koray Kavukcuoglu, an executive more closely associated with product delivery and commercial integration, will run the organization.</span></p><p><span>Losing your very best talent in a short span, both homegrown in the case of Dean and Ghemawat, and acquired in the case of Hassabis, looks like bad news. Superstars like to be on the winning team, after all.</span></p><p><span>This is what the market believed, and Alphabet&#8217;s share price dropped 4% in a day. </span></p><p><span>But in our view, this is as much a signal about capital and compute allocation as it is about talent.</span></p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Pq6Q!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fde2c23e8-231b-4f06-b70a-86c5198452ff_2700x1500.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Pq6Q!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fde2c23e8-231b-4f06-b70a-86c5198452ff_2700x1500.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Pq6Q!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fde2c23e8-231b-4f06-b70a-86c5198452ff_2700x1500.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Pq6Q!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fde2c23e8-231b-4f06-b70a-86c5198452ff_2700x1500.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Pq6Q!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fde2c23e8-231b-4f06-b70a-86c5198452ff_2700x1500.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Pq6Q!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fde2c23e8-231b-4f06-b70a-86c5198452ff_2700x1500.png" width="1456" height="809" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/de2c23e8-231b-4f06-b70a-86c5198452ff_2700x1500.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:809,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:368001,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://www.exponentialview.co/i/211191094?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fde2c23e8-231b-4f06-b70a-86c5198452ff_2700x1500.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Pq6Q!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fde2c23e8-231b-4f06-b70a-86c5198452ff_2700x1500.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Pq6Q!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fde2c23e8-231b-4f06-b70a-86c5198452ff_2700x1500.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Pq6Q!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fde2c23e8-231b-4f06-b70a-86c5198452ff_2700x1500.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Pq6Q!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fde2c23e8-231b-4f06-b70a-86c5198452ff_2700x1500.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>That matters because Alphabet is not an ordinary incumbent. Google built the most formidable system in corporate history for stewarding uncertain ideas from the demands of its cash-generating core. Think of 20% time; it&#8217;s moonshot factory, X; the Alphabet corporate structure; and an extraordinary appetite to acquire.</p><p>If even Google now allows the engineers who built its very foundations to leave, something about the way it allocates capital has changed. The question is what. Are researchers leaving Alphabet because they lost faith in the firm&#8217;s AI prospects? Or because every  TPU can earn such an attractive return serving today&#8217;s bread-and-butter models that open-ended research fails to clear the hurdle? </p><p>These imply opposite positions in the AI capital cycle.</p><p>Below, we identify how Google&#8217;s compute has moved, examine what demand for old chips reveals about the economic lives of AI chips, and identify the four signals that would tell us the infrastructure cycle has finally turned.</p><h3><mark data-color="#fff2cc" style="background-color: rgb(255, 242, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Continue reading: seven charts and our AI-cycle call</mark></h3><p>Markets viewed these departures as a crisis. We think they tell us more about the capital-compute axis.</p><p>The full essay includes seven charts showing:</p><ul><li><p>How Google&#8217;s latest models fare on the Pareto frontier</p></li><li><p>How it has shifted compute away from research</p></li><li><p>What Google Cloud&#8217;s growth and economics reveal about infrastructure demand.</p></li><li><p>Where we are in the AI infrastructure cycle&#8230; and the four signals that would tell us it has finally turned.</p></li></ul><p><strong><mark data-color="#fff2cc" style="background-color: rgb(255, 242, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Upgrade to continue reading.</mark></strong></p>
